From bc6a3cc502293ec31fd360cc169908f3704feb4a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justin <justurn@live.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 03:47:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Zeppelin F-223: MinimapForceTileReload sets the minimap dirty
 bit

MinimapUpdate skips its tile pass unless the player moved in x/y or
s_updateFlags bit 0 is set, so a phase change while standing still kept the
base tiles (WXL sets the same bit, its kDirtyTiles).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01ByrZ7GxoHC9wfGdkRwtqCX
---
 WoW/Source/Ui/MinimapFrame.cpp | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/WoW/Source/Ui/MinimapFrame.cpp b/WoW/Source/Ui/MinimapFrame.cpp
index 681ca82..4afb2de 100644
--- a/WoW/Source/Ui/MinimapFrame.cpp
+++ b/WoW/Source/Ui/MinimapFrame.cpp
@@ -1253,6 +1253,8 @@ static bool s_forceTileReload;
 // extension that changed the art a tile resolves to without the map id changing (a terrain phase).
 void MinimapForceTileReload() {
     s_forceTileReload = true;
+    // MinimapUpdate skips the tile pass unless the player moved in x/y or this bit is set.
+    s_updateFlags |= 1;
 }
 
 // VERIFY: dd828e8c manual
